From: DoubleGate <parobek@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 05:34:54 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] [UPSTREAM] check: recording-level permanent-identity-exposure
 summary (T-OR-060)

rayhunter-check now tallies, per recording, how often the network obtained or
targeted a UE's permanent identity (IMSI/IMEI): events from the identity
disclosure, IMSI-requested and IMSI-paging analyzers, grouped by analyzer. The
count appears in the stdout summary and as an `identity_exposure` map in the
JSON report (empty when nothing exposed an identity), so an operator can gauge
a recording's exposure without grepping every event.

This is a report-side aggregate over events the harness already produces -- no
analyzer-trait or analysis change. Also moves the check test module to the end
of the file so the crate is clippy-clean (items-after-test-module).

Test: the tally counts only the identity-exposure analyzers (a non-identity
analyzer does not contribute) and groups repeats per analyzer.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: DoubleGate <parobek@gmail.com>
---
 check/src/main.rs | 135 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-----------
 1 file changed, 104 insertions(+), 31 deletions(-)

diff --git a/check/src/main.rs b/check/src/main.rs
index 94c3429..2f88a27 100644
--- a/check/src/main.rs
+++ b/check/src/main.rs
@@ -10,7 +10,10 @@ use rayhunter::{
     qmdl::QmdlMessageReader,
 };
 use serde::{Deserialize, Serialize};
-use std::{collections::HashMap, path::PathBuf};
+use std::{
+    collections::{BTreeMap, HashMap},
+    path::PathBuf,
+};
 use tokio::fs::File;
 use walkdir::WalkDir;
 
@@ -57,6 +60,15 @@ struct EventWithTimestamp {
     event: Event,
 }
 
+/// Analyzers whose firing means the network obtained or targeted a UE's
+/// PERMANENT identity (IMSI/IMEI), the exposure T-OR-060 summarises per
+/// recording. Matched by analyzer name (`Analyzer::get_name`).
+const IDENTITY_EXPOSURE_ANALYZERS: &[&str] = &[
+    "Identity (IMSI or IMEI) requested in suspicious manner",
+    "Permanent identity disclosure",
+    "IMSI paging",
+];
+
 #[derive(Debug, Default, Serialize, Deserialize, PartialEq)]
 struct Report {
     skipped_reasons: HashMap<String, u32>,
@@ -64,6 +76,10 @@ struct Report {
     total_messages: u32,
     warnings: u32,
     skipped: u32,
+    /// Per-recording count of permanent-identity-exposure events, keyed by
+    /// analyzer name (T-OR-060). Empty when nothing exposed an identity.
+    #[serde(default)]
+    identity_exposure: BTreeMap<String, u32>,
     file_path: String,
 }
 
@@ -103,6 +119,9 @@ impl Report {
                     self.warnings += 1;
                 }
             }
+            if IDENTITY_EXPOSURE_ANALYZERS.contains(&analyzer.as_str()) {
+                *self.identity_exposure.entry(analyzer.clone()).or_insert(0) += 1;
+            }
             self.events.push(EventWithTimestamp {
                 timestamp,
                 analyzer,
@@ -122,36 +141,20 @@ impl Report {
             "{}: {} messages analyzed, {} warnings, {} messages skipped",
             self.file_path, self.total_messages, self.warnings, self.skipped
         );
-    }
-}
